# Day 10 — First Frost. 13 September. Frost and morning mist, then clear and cold.
# The closing checklist. Packing up Augie's cabin. Dot hasn't decided about Calder.

call D10_AM
  day 10
  time 06:20-12:00
  kind report
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. Tell me there's frost.
choice
  > "There's frost on the meadow. White all over." -> frost
  > "Dry {dry}, wet {wet}. Wind {wind}." if obs_am set gave_readings -> read
node frost
THEO Basin, Kestrel. There's frost on the whole meadow. It's white all over, down to the creek.
DOT  ...I've always wanted to see that.
goto plan
node read
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Dry bulb {dry}, wet {wet}. Humidity {rh}. Wind {wind}. Fuel stick {fuel}. Frost on the meadow.
DOT  Copy. Fuel stick's finally wet. That's the season, nearly.
node plan
DOT  Last truck brought a list. It's in my capitals, so you know I mean it.
DOT  Shutters on the cabin. Drain the cistern at the tower. Leave the logbook for whoever's next.
do errand Closing chores: put the shutters up on Pell's Cabin and drain the cistern at the tower.

call D10_CABIN
  day 10
  where cabin
  after D10_AM
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. You're at the cabin.
THEO I'm packing his things. There isn't much.
DOT  Tell me what's there.
THEO The flower book. A drawer with a letter he never sent. Spoons on a string. A jar of buttons.
DOT  ...Take nothing. It's his.
DOT  ...Except the flower book. Would you bring me the flower book?
choice
  > "I'll bring it." set flower_book -> bring
  > "I'll leave it for him." -> leave
node bring
THEO I'll bring it.
DOT  Thank you. I'll give it back to him. I'll — I'll give it back. Basin out.
end
node leave
THEO I'll leave it for him. It belongs here.
DOT  You're right. You're right. Basin out.

call D10_CHORES
  day 10
  needs shutters_done, cistern_done
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. Shutters? Cistern?
THEO Shutters up. Cistern drained. The tower sounds hollow now.
DOT  That's the season put away. Nearly.
do errand_done
DOT  Basin out.

call D10_EVE
  day 10
  time 16:30-18:30
  retry 20:00
  kind report
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. Last-but-one evening readings.
choice
  > "Dry {dry}, wet {wet}. Wind {wind}." if obs_pm set gave_readings -> read
  > "I didn't go out." -> no
node read
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Dry {dry}, wet {wet}. Humidity {rh}. Wind {wind}.
DOT  Copy. Barometer's dropping down here. Something's coming. Basin out.
end
node no
THEO I didn't go out.
DOT  Barometer's dropping down here anyway. Something's coming. Basin out.

call D10_NIGHT
  day 10
  time 21:00-26:00
DOT  Kestrel, Basin.
THEO Dot.
DOT  You're going to ask me about Calder.
THEO I wasn't going to.
DOT  You were. You've got a way of not asking that's louder than asking.
DOT  I haven't decided. Ask me tomorrow. ...No. Don't.
choice
  > "I won't." -> wont
  > "Ruth's piano's waiting either way." if offered_tuning -> piano
  > [say nothing] -> quiet
node wont
THEO I won't.
DOT  Goodnight, Theo.
end
node piano
THEO Ruth's piano is waiting either way.
DOT  ...Goodnight, Theo.
end
node quiet
DOT  Goodnight, Theo.
